# atlas keeps its own ignores now.
#
# Until the split (2026-09-10) every one of these lines lived in the ground's
# .gitignore, one directory up, and atlas had no file of its own. The moment
# atlas became its own repository that file stopped applying to it, and the
# next `git add -A` here would have committed two .exe binaries, three logs,
# a server's data directory and the seat log. These lines are carried across
# unchanged in meaning, rewritten to be relative to this repository's root.

# Build output. The source is 4.5 MB; a cargo build drops a 456 MB target/
# beside it and `go build` leaves .exe in line/ and webapp/. None of it is
# source and none of it goes in the record.
target/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.obj

# The two servers' own stdout AND stderr. atlas-mcp and atlas-webapp are
# started by hand, and a doc that tells him to run a command which dirties his
# repo is a bad doc.
#
# mcp.err joined them 2026-09-10: starting the door with PowerShell's
# -RedirectStandardError splits stderr into its own file, and the door writes
# a failed env_open there (engine.go's Registry.Open). That line is the thing
# that finally made a hung boot diagnosable -- so the file earns its place on
# disk and has no business in the record.
line/mcp.log
line/mcp.err
webapp/web.log
webapp/web.err

# The webapp's own store. Written at runtime, never authored.
webapp/data/

# The ledger is written at every open, toll, land and close, so a tracked copy
# makes the ground DIRTY before he types a word. Operator's ruling 2026-09-08:
# "dont git track them." It stays on disk as the record; git holds the code and
# the docs.
SEAT_LOG.md

# Keys are silent (LAW 9).
.env

# Fetched, never authored.
node_modules/
.venv/

# Python's own build output. THE BALL (tests/prove.py) imports nothing, but it
# RUNS twenty-seven cutters and six workflow scripts, and every one of those
# leaves a __pycache__ beside itself. Added 2026-09-10, the first time the
# whole battery was run in one command and the tree came back dirty for it.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
